The code statements that fix the bug are:
pwlan = rtw_find_network(&pmlmepriv->scanned_queue, tgt_network->network.mac_address);
if (!pwlan)
	return;
pwlan->fixed = false;
rtw_free_network_nolock(adapter, pwlan);
Reason:
By adding an early return when `pwlan` is NULL, the function avoids any further use of the null pointer, including the `rtw_free_network_nolock` call that would dereference it. This ensures safe handling of the NULL case.

